  TUL STRICT GEOMETRY ON (coda_prefix_reach=all): the prelude is same-span ONLY, a coda prefix cell reads itself alone, the conv/value-shift and the retention carry reset at every segment, and the coda's per-layer injections at the slot cells are zeroed — the slot LOOP is the only cross-span channel (lab/experiments/planned/2026-09-12-arc-strict-geometry.md)
  TUL SLOT-CELL PASS NORM 'rms' ON: after EVERY slot-loop pass each carried cell is RMSNorm(h) * g (per Hyper-Connection stream over the channels, eps 1e-6, ONE learned gain g shared by every pass, init 1.0, no-decay, never ternary); the entry state is NOT normed. The fixed-point term compares normed states; the latent head, the teacher, the diversity term and the prefix write read the normed cell. NOTE the gain hinge (model.slot_gain_lambda=100.0) still reads the RAW map f, not the normed map the loop carries: it bounds f, not the carried gain - read val/slot_cell_rms_t{t} (should sit at rms(g)) and val/slot_cell_norm_g_mean / _std
  TG SCOPED KERNELS ON: HC-Cayley + CCA prologue + core window fused; TG-restricted attention branches eager by construction; CE chunked
